COMMAND NAME: mppcrondump.sh

A wrapper script for mpp_dump, which can be called from a crontab entry.


*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mppcrondump.sh -x <database_name> [-s <schema_name>] [-d 
<master_data_directory>] [-p | -m] [-c | -o] [-z] [-r] [-f 
<free_space_percent>] [-b] [-i] [-j] [-k] [-a] [-q] [-l <logfile_directory>]

mppcrondump.sh -? | -v


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

mppcrondump.sh is a wrapper script for mpp_dump. It allows you to schedule 
routine backups of a Bizgres MPP database using cron (a scheduling utility 
for Linux and Unix operating systems). Cron jobs that call mppcrondump.sh 
should be scheduled on the MPP master host.

Here is an example of the crontab file, which schedules a nightly dump of the 
customers database at one minute past midnight. Note that the SHELL is set to 
/bin/bash and the PATH includes the location of the Bizgres MPP management 
scripts  this is required to run mppcrondump.sh. 

SHELL=/bin/bash

PATH=/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:$MPPHOME/mppMgmt/bin

MAILTO=bgadmin

HOME=/home/bgadmin



# Bizgres MPP nightly database dump job

01 0 * * * bgadmin mppcrondump.sh -x customers -a -q >> 
mpp_custdump.log


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-x <database_name>

Required. The name of the Bizgres MPP database to dump.


-s <schema_name>

Optional. Dump only the named schema in the named database.


-d <master_data_directory>

Optional. The master host data directory. If not specified, the value set for 
$MASTER_DATA_DIRECTORY will be used.


-p

Optional. Dump the primary segment instances only. The default is to dump both 
primary and mirror segment instances. 


-m

Optional. Dump the mirror segment instances only. The default is to dump both 
primary and mirror segment instances.


-c

Clear out old dump files before doing the dump. The default is not to clear 
out old dump files. 


-o

Clear out old dump files only, but do not run a dump. 


-z

Do not use compression. Default is to compress the dump files.


-r

Do not rollback the dump files if a failure is detected. The default is to 
rollback.


-f <free_space_percent>

Percentage of free disk space to reserve when calculating the available free 
disk space for the dump operation. The default is 10.


-b

Bypass disk space check. The default is to check for available disk space.


-i

Ignore the initial parameter check phase.


-j

Run VACUUM before the dump starts.


-k

Run VACUUM after the dump has completed sucessfully.


-a

Do not prompt the user for confirmation.


-q

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, but is still 
written to the log file.


-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/mppAdminLogs.


-?

Displays the online help.


-v

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum of this script.


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

A crontab file that runs a backup of the sales database nightly at one past 
midnight:

SHELL=/bin/bash

PATH=/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:$MPPHOME/mppMgmt/bin

01 0 * * * bgadmin mppcrondump.sh -x customers -a -q >> 
mpp_custdump.log


